# THE NOTES DEMO'S LAWS, each a CLAIM (a `rule` with no `show`) proven by the task of its name, so the kernel checks
# the proof as one term and keeps it for the Lean export. A law's lemmas are claims too, named after the law, so a
# broken model is refused under the law's name.
#
# THE LAWS ARE STATED OVER RELATIONS (`steps s e t`: event e takes state s to t), and model.tree's tasks are tied to
# them by BRIDGE claims at the end of this file: `view-shows` says what `view` computes is a view `shows` allows, so
# laws 4 and 5 hold of the task itself (`deleted-stays-gone-of-view`, `isolation-of-view`). A claim's type may call a
# pure, terminating task of the program since term-proof-0004, which the kernel unfolds. The bridges for `step` and
# `replay` (law 1 of the task) are not written yet. The relations are nondeterministic where safety allows: an erase
# may always leave a note as it was, a view may always leave a note out, so each law holds of every way to resolve
# them. The forms are model.tree's, so a law and the task it is about name one `shelf`.
load ./model
  find natural
  find rank
  find person
  find note
  find shelf
  find event
  find events
  find flag
  find same
  find view
  find pick
  find show
  find step
  find cross
  find settle
  find aim
  find guard
  find may
  find replay

# THE POLICY: a person may erase a note when the person is an admin, or owns it
form allowed
  head by, like person
  head whose, like natural
  case as-admin
    link i, like natural
    link w, like natural
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, make admin
    head
      read w
  case as-owner
    link w, like natural
    link r, like rank
    head
      make person
        bind id, w
        bind rank, r
    head
      read w

# ONE NOTE UNDER AN ERASE by `actor` of note `id`: n becomes m
form settles
  head n, like note
  head actor, like person
  head id, like natural
  head m, like note
  # the note named, and the policy allows it: it is buried, by the actor
  case hit
    link at, like natural
    link whose, like natural
    link doer, like person
    link allowed-by
      like allowed
        head
          read doer
        head
          read whose
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
    head
      read doer
    head
      read at
    head
      make gone
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
        bind by, doer
  # any live note may stay as it was: another note, or a refusal
  case keep
    link at, like natural
    link whose, like natural
    link doer, like person
    link aim, like natural
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
    head
      read doer
    head
      read aim
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
  # a gone note stays gone
  case still
    link at, like natural
    link whose, like natural
    link by, like person
    link doer, like person
    link aim, like natural
    head
      make gone
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
        bind by, by
    head
      read doer
    head
      read aim
    head
      make gone
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
        bind by, by

# THE WHOLE SHELF UNDER AN ERASE: each note settles
form crosses
  head s, like shelf
  head actor, like person
  head id, like natural
  head t, like shelf
  case cross-end
    link doer, like person
    link aim, like natural
    head
      make bare
    head
      read doer
    head
      read aim
    head
      make bare
  case cross-on
    link top, like note
    link rest, like shelf
    link doer, like person
    link aim, like natural
    link top-after, like note
    link rest-after, like shelf
    link one
      like settles
        head
          read top
        head
          read doer
        head
          read aim
        head
          read top-after
    link others
      like crosses
        head
          read rest
        head
          read doer
        head
          read aim
        head
          read rest-after
    head
      make more
        bind top, top
        bind rest, rest
    head
      read doer
    head
      read aim
    head
      make more
        bind top, top-after
        bind rest, rest-after

# STEP: event e takes state s to t
form steps
  head s, like shelf
  head e, like event
  head t, like shelf
  # a write puts a live note, owned by the writer, on the shelf
  case wrote
    link before, like shelf
    link i, like natural
    link r, like rank
    link aim, like natural
    head
      read before
    head
      make write
        bind who, i
        bind rank, r
        bind id, aim
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make live
            bind at, aim
            bind whose, i
        bind rest, before
  # an erase by the person the event names crosses the whole shelf
  case erased
    link before, like shelf
    link i, like natural
    link r, like rank
    link aim, like natural
    link after-erase, like shelf
    link crossing
      like crosses
        head
          read before
        head
          make person
            bind id, i
            bind rank, r
        head
          read aim
        head
          read after-erase
    head
      read before
    head
      make erase
        bind who, i
        bind rank, r
        bind id, aim
    head
      read after-erase

# REPLAY: the events es, from the empty shelf, reach s
form replays
  head es, like events
  head s, like shelf
  case from-start
    head
      make begin
    head
      make bare
  case then
    link last, like event
    link sooner, like events
    link was, like shelf
    link now, like shelf
    link reached
      like replays
        head
          read sooner
        head
          read was
    link stepped
      like steps
        head
          read was
        head
          read last
        head
          read now
    head
      make after
        bind event, last
        bind earlier, sooner
    head
      read now

# VIEW: what `viewer` is shown of shelf s is v. A person sees their own live notes, and any note may be left out
form shows
  head s, like shelf
  head viewer, like person
  head v, like shelf
  case show-end
    link doer, like person
    head
      make bare
    head
      read doer
    head
      make bare
  case show-own
    link at, like natural
    link w, like natural
    link r, like rank
    link rest, like shelf
    link shown, like shelf
    link others
      like shows
        head
          read rest
        head
          make person
            bind id, w
            bind rank, r
        head
          read shown
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, w
        bind rest, rest
    head
      make person
        bind id, w
        bind rank, r
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, w
        bind rest, shown
  case show-skip
    link n, like note
    link rest, like shelf
    link doer, like person
    link shown, like shelf
    link others
      like shows
        head
          read rest
        head
          read doer
        head
          read shown
    head
      make more
        bind top, n
        bind rest, rest
    head
      read doer
    head
      read shown

# every note on the shelf is live
form all-live
  head v, like shelf
  case live-end
    head
      make bare
  case live-on
    link at, like natural
    link whose, like natural
    link rest, like shelf
    link rest-live
      like all-live
        head
          read rest
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, whose
        bind rest, rest

# every note on the shelf is owned by `who`, live or gone
form owned
  head who, like person
  head v, like shelf
  case owned-end
    link doer, like person
    head
      read doer
    head
      make bare
  case owned-live
    link at, like natural
    link w, like natural
    link r, like rank
    link rest, like shelf
    link rest-owned
      like owned
        head
          make person
            bind id, w
            bind rank, r
        head
          read rest
    head
      make person
        bind id, w
        bind rank, r
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, w
        bind rest, rest
  case owned-gone
    link at, like natural
    link w, like natural
    link r, like rank
    link by, like person
    link rest, like shelf
    link rest-owned
      like owned
        head
          make person
            bind id, w
            bind rank, r
        head
          read rest
    head
      make person
        bind id, w
        bind rank, r
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make gone
            bind at, at
            bind whose, w
            bind by, by
        bind rest, rest

# LAW 4, DELETED STAYS GONE: no view of any state shows an erased note.
rule deleted-stays-gone
  take s, like shelf
  take viewer, like person
  take v, like shelf
  take seen
    like shows
      head
        read s
      head
        read viewer
      head
        read v
  like all-live
    head
      read v

task deleted-stays-gone
  take s
  take viewer
  take v
  take seen
  sift seen
    case show-end
      back make live-end
    case show-own
      back
        make live-on
          bind at, at
          bind whose, w
          bind rest, shown
          bind rest-live
            deleted-stays-gone
              read rest
              make person
                bind id, w
                bind rank, r
              read shown
              read others
    case show-skip
      back deleted-stays-gone(rest, doer, shown, others)

# LAW 5, ISOLATION: a person's view never shows another person's note.
rule isolation
  take s, like shelf
  take viewer, like person
  take v, like shelf
  take seen
    like shows
      head
        read s
      head
        read viewer
      head
        read v
  like owned
    head
      read viewer
    head
      read v

task isolation
  take s
  take viewer
  take v
  take seen
  sift seen
    case show-end
      back
        make owned-end
          bind doer, doer
    case show-own
      back
        make owned-live
          bind at, at
          bind w, w
          bind r, r
          bind rest, shown
          bind rest-owned
            isolation
              read rest
              make person
                bind id, w
                bind rank, r
              read shown
              read others
    case show-skip
      back isolation(rest, doer, shown, others)

# A FAIR note: live, or gone by someone the policy allowed
form fair
  head n, like note
  case fresh
    link at, like natural
    link whose, like natural
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
  case buried
    link at, like natural
    link whose, like natural
    link by, like person
    link allowed-by
      like allowed
        head
          read by
        head
          read whose
    head
      make gone
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
        bind by, by

form fair-shelf
  head s, like shelf
  case clean
    head
      make bare
  case also
    link top, like note
    link rest, like shelf
    link top-fair
      like fair
        head
          read top
    link rest-fair
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read rest
    head
      make more
        bind top, top
        bind rest, rest

# LAW 1, OWNERSHIP: after any sequence of events, every erased note was erased by its owner or an admin.
rule ownership
  take es, like events
  take s, like shelf
  take run
    like replays
      head
        read es
      head
        read s
  like fair-shelf
    head
      read s

task ownership
  take es
  take s
  take run
  sift run
    case from-start
      back make clean
    case then
      back ownership-carry(was, now, ownership-step(was, last, now, stepped), ownership(sooner, was, reached))

# apply a step's preservation to the evidence before it
rule ownership-carry
  take a, like shelf
  take b, like shelf
  take keep
    like task
      take ok
        like fair-shelf
          head
            read a
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read b
  take x
    like fair-shelf
      head
        read a
  like fair-shelf
    head
      read b

task ownership-carry
  take a
  take b
  take keep
  take x
  back keep(x)

# one step keeps every note fair. THE CONVOY: the shelf's evidence is taken after the match, so the match rewrites it
rule ownership-step
  take s, like shelf
  take e, like event
  take t, like shelf
  take st
    like steps
      head
        read s
      head
        read e
      head
        read t
  like task
    take ok
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read s
    like fair-shelf
      head
        read t

task ownership-step
  take s
  take e
  take t
  take st
  sift st
    case wrote
      back
        task
          take ok
            like fair-shelf
              head
                read before
          like fair-shelf
            head
              make more
                bind top
                  make live
                    bind at, aim
                    bind whose, i
                bind rest, before
          back
            make also
              bind top
                make live
                  bind at, aim
                  bind whose, i
              bind rest, before
              bind top-fair
                make fresh
                  bind at, aim
                  bind whose, i
              bind rest-fair, ok
    case erased
      back
        ownership-cross
          read before
          make person
            bind id, i
            bind rank, r
          read aim
          read after-erase
          read crossing

rule ownership-cross
  take s, like shelf
  take actor, like person
  take id, like natural
  take t, like shelf
  take c
    like crosses
      head
        read s
      head
        read actor
      head
        read id
      head
        read t
  like task
    take ok
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read s
    like fair-shelf
      head
        read t

task ownership-cross
  take s
  take actor
  take id
  take t
  take c
  sift c
    case cross-end
      back
        task
          take ok
            like fair-shelf
              head
                make bare
          like fair-shelf
            head
              make bare
          back make clean
    case cross-on
      back
        ownership-join
          read top
          read rest
          read top-after
          read rest-after
          ownership-settle(top, doer, aim, top-after, one)
          ownership-cross(rest, doer, aim, rest-after, others)

# a fair shelf whose top and rest each stay fair stays fair
rule ownership-join
  take a, like note
  take r, like shelf
  take a2, like note
  take r2, like shelf
  take keep-top
    like task
      take ok
        like fair
          head
            read a
      like fair
        head
          read a2
  take keep-rest
    like task
      take ok
        like fair-shelf
          head
            read r
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read r2
  like task
    take ok
      like fair-shelf
        head
          make more
            bind top, a
            bind rest, r
    like fair-shelf
      head
        make more
          bind top, a2
          bind rest, r2

task ownership-join
  take a
  take r
  take a2
  take r2
  take keep-top
  take keep-rest
  back
    task
      take ok
        like fair-shelf
          head
            make more
              bind top, a
              bind rest, r
      like fair-shelf
        head
          make more
            bind top, a2
            bind rest, r2
      back ownership-apply(a, r, a2, r2, ownership-split(a, r, a2, r2, ok), keep-top, keep-rest)

# THE MATCH on a fair shelf that is not empty: its one case is `also`. A convoy, so the match rewrites the two keeps
rule ownership-split
  take a, like note
  take r, like shelf
  take a2, like note
  take r2, like shelf
  take ok
    like fair-shelf
      head
        make more
          bind top, a
          bind rest, r
  like task
    take keep-top
      like task
        take ok
          like fair
            head
              read a
        like fair
          head
            read a2
    take keep-rest
      like task
        take ok
          like fair-shelf
            head
              read r
        like fair-shelf
          head
            read r2
    like fair-shelf
      head
        make more
          bind top, a2
          bind rest, r2

task ownership-split
  take a
  take r
  take a2
  take r2
  take ok
  sift ok
    case also
      back
        task
          take keep-top
            like task
              take ok
                like fair
                  head
                    read top
              like fair
                head
                  read a2
          take keep-rest
            like task
              take ok
                like fair-shelf
                  head
                    read rest
              like fair-shelf
                head
                  read r2
          like fair-shelf
            head
              make more
                bind top, a2
                bind rest, r2
          back ownership-build(top, rest, a2, r2, keep-top, keep-rest, top-fair, rest-fair)

# a proof may call a parameter of its task, not of a `task` written inside it, so the keeps are called here
rule ownership-build
  take a, like note
  take r, like shelf
  take a2, like note
  take r2, like shelf
  take keep-top
    like task
      take ok
        like fair
          head
            read a
      like fair
        head
          read a2
  take keep-rest
    like task
      take ok
        like fair-shelf
          head
            read r
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read r2
  take top-was
    like fair
      head
        read a
  take rest-was
    like fair-shelf
      head
        read r
  like fair-shelf
    head
      make more
        bind top, a2
        bind rest, r2

task ownership-build
  take a
  take r
  take a2
  take r2
  take keep-top
  take keep-rest
  take top-was
  take rest-was
  back
    make also
      bind top, a2
      bind rest, r2
      bind top-fair, keep-top(top-was)
      bind rest-fair, keep-rest(rest-was)

rule ownership-apply
  take a, like note
  take r, like shelf
  take a2, like note
  take r2, like shelf
  take join
    like task
      take keep-top
        like task
          take ok
            like fair
              head
                read a
          like fair
            head
              read a2
      take keep-rest
        like task
          take ok
            like fair-shelf
              head
                read r
          like fair-shelf
            head
              read r2
      like fair-shelf
        head
          make more
            bind top, a2
            bind rest, r2
  take keep-top
    like task
      take ok
        like fair
          head
            read a
      like fair
        head
          read a2
  take keep-rest
    like task
      take ok
        like fair-shelf
          head
            read r
      like fair-shelf
        head
          read r2
  like fair-shelf
    head
      make more
        bind top, a2
        bind rest, r2

task ownership-apply
  take a
  take r
  take a2
  take r2
  take join
  take keep-top
  take keep-rest
  back join(keep-top, keep-rest)

rule ownership-settle
  take n, like note
  take actor, like person
  take id, like natural
  take m, like note
  take st
    like settles
      head
        read n
      head
        read actor
      head
        read id
      head
        read m
  like task
    take ok
      like fair
        head
          read n
    like fair
      head
        read m

task ownership-settle
  take n
  take actor
  take id
  take m
  take st
  sift st
    case hit
      back
        task
          take ok
            like fair
              head
                make live
                  bind at, at
                  bind whose, whose
          like fair
            head
              make gone
                bind at, at
                bind whose, whose
                bind by, doer
          back
            make buried
              bind at, at
              bind whose, whose
              bind by, doer
              bind allowed-by, allowed-by
    case keep
      back
        task
          take ok
            like fair
              head
                make live
                  bind at, at
                  bind whose, whose
          like fair
            head
              make live
                bind at, at
                bind whose, whose
          back ok
    case still
      back
        task
          take ok
            like fair
              head
                make gone
                  bind at, at
                  bind whose, whose
                  bind by, by
          like fair
            head
              make gone
                bind at, at
                bind whose, whose
                bind by, by
          back ok

# ---- THE BRIDGE FOR VIEW: model.tree's `view` computes a view `shows` allows ----

# what `same(w, i)` answers, as evidence: `yes` only where w is i
form same-view
  head w, like natural
  head i, like natural
  head f, like flag
  case is-same
    link k, like natural
    head
      read k
    head
      read k
    head
      make yes
  case not-same
    link a, like natural
    link b, like natural
    head
      read a
    head
      read b
    head
      make no

# a step down both naturals keeps the evidence
rule view-same-lift
  take p, like natural
  take q, like natural
  take f, like flag
  take ev
    like same-view
      head
        read p
      head
        read q
      head
        read f
  like same-view
    head
      make succ
        bind prior, p
    head
      make succ
        bind prior, q
    head
      read f

task view-same-lift
  take p
  take q
  take f
  take ev
  sift ev
    case is-same
      back
        make is-same
          bind k
            make succ
              bind prior, k
    case not-same
      back
        make not-same
          bind a
            make succ
              bind prior, a
          bind b
            make succ
              bind prior, b

# `same` answers as the evidence says
rule view-same
  take w, like natural
  take i, like natural
  like same-view
    head
      read w
    head
      read i
    head
      same(w, i)

task view-same
  take w
  take i
  sift w
    case zero
      back view-same-zero(i)
    case succ
      link p
      back
        view-same-succ
          read p
          read i
          task
            take q, like natural
            like same-view
              head
                read p
              head
                read q
              head
                same(p, q)
            back view-same(p, q)

rule view-same-zero
  take i, like natural
  like same-view
    head
      make zero
    head
      read i
    head
      same
        make zero
        read i

task view-same-zero
  take i
  sift i
    case zero
      back
        make is-same
          bind k, make zero
    case succ
      back
        make not-same
          bind a, make zero
          bind b
            make succ
              bind prior, prior

rule view-same-succ
  take p, like natural
  take i, like natural
  take below
    like task
      take q, like natural
      like same-view
        head
          read p
        head
          read q
        head
          same(p, q)
  like same-view
    head
      make succ
        bind prior, p
    head
      read i
    head
      same
        make succ
          bind prior, p
        read i

task view-same-succ
  take p
  take i
  take below
  sift i
    case zero
      back
        make not-same
          bind a
            make succ
              bind prior, p
          bind b, make zero
    case succ
      link q
      back view-same-lift(p, q, same(p, q), below(q))

# ONE LIVE NOTE BEFORE A VIEW: shown when `same` said yes, skipped when it said no. A convoy: the rest's view is taken
# after the match, so the match rewrites the viewer's id in its type
rule view-pick-by
  take at, like natural
  take r, like rank
  take rest, like shelf
  take shown, like shelf
  take w, like natural
  take i, like natural
  take f, like flag
  take ev
    like same-view
      head
        read w
      head
        read i
      head
        read f
  like task
    take others
      like shows
        head
          read rest
        head
          make person
            bind id, i
            bind rank, r
        head
          read shown
    like shows
      head
        make more
          bind top
            make live
              bind at, at
              bind whose, w
          bind rest, rest
      head
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
      head
        show
          read f
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, w
          read shown

task view-pick-by
  take at
  take r
  take rest
  take shown
  take w
  take i
  take f
  take ev
  sift ev
    case is-same
      back
        task
          take others
            like shows
              head
                read rest
              head
                make person
                  bind id, k
                  bind rank, r
              head
                read shown
          like shows
            head
              make more
                bind top
                  make live
                    bind at, at
                    bind whose, k
                bind rest, rest
            head
              make person
                bind id, k
                bind rank, r
            head
              make more
                bind top
                  make live
                    bind at, at
                    bind whose, k
                bind rest, shown
          back
            make show-own
              bind at, at
              bind w, k
              bind r, r
              bind rest, rest
              bind shown, shown
              bind others, others
    case not-same
      back
        task
          take others
            like shows
              head
                read rest
              head
                make person
                  bind id, b
                  bind rank, r
              head
                read shown
          like shows
            head
              make more
                bind top
                  make live
                    bind at, at
                    bind whose, a
                bind rest, rest
            head
              make person
                bind id, b
                bind rank, r
            head
              read shown
          back
            make show-skip
              bind n
                make live
                  bind at, at
                  bind whose, a
              bind rest, rest
              bind doer
                make person
                  bind id, b
                  bind rank, r
              bind shown, shown
              bind others, others

# ONE LIVE NOTE BEFORE A VIEW, by what `same` answers. Its type is written through `pick`, which computes to
# `show(same(whose, i), ...)`, the type `view-pick-by` builds
rule view-pick-live
  take at, like natural
  take whose, like natural
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  take rest, like shelf
  take shown, like shelf
  take others
    like shows
      head
        read rest
      head
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
      head
        read shown
  like shows
    head
      make more
        bind top
          make live
            bind at, at
            bind whose, whose
        bind rest, rest
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      pick
        make live
          bind at, at
          bind whose, whose
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
        read shown

task view-pick-live
  take at
  take whose
  take i
  take r
  take rest
  take shown
  take others
  save fill, view-pick-by(at, r, rest, shown, whose, i, same(whose, i), view-same(whose, i))
  back fill(others)

# ONE NOTE BEFORE A VIEW, live or gone
rule view-pick
  take top, like note
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  take rest, like shelf
  take shown, like shelf
  take others
    like shows
      head
        read rest
      head
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
      head
        read shown
  like shows
    head
      make more
        bind top, top
        bind rest, rest
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      pick
        read top
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
        read shown

task view-pick
  take top
  take i
  take r
  take rest
  take shown
  take others
  sift top
    case live
      back view-pick-live(at, whose, i, r, rest, shown, others)
    case gone
      back
        make show-skip
          bind n
            make gone
              bind at, at
              bind whose, whose
              bind by, by
          bind rest, rest
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
          bind shown, shown
          bind others, others

# THE BRIDGE: what `view` computes for the viewer `person(i, r)` is a view `shows` allows
rule view-shows
  take s, like shelf
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  like shows
    head
      read s
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      view
        read s
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r

task view-shows
  take s
  take i
  take r
  sift s
    case bare
      back
        make show-end
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
    case more
      back
        view-pick
          read top
          read i
          read r
          read rest
          view
            read rest
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
          view-shows(rest, i, r)

# LAW 4 OF THE TASK: no view `view` computes shows an erased note
rule deleted-stays-gone-of-view
  take s, like shelf
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  like all-live
    head
      view
        read s
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r

task deleted-stays-gone-of-view
  take s
  take i
  take r
  back
    deleted-stays-gone
      read s
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
      view
        read s
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
      view-shows(s, i, r)

# LAW 5 OF THE TASK: every note `view` computes for a person is that person's
rule isolation-of-view
  take s, like shelf
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  like owned
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      view
        read s
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r

task isolation-of-view
  take s
  take i
  take r
  back
    isolation
      read s
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
      view
        read s
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
      view-shows(s, i, r)

# ---- THE BRIDGE FOR REPLAY: model.tree's `step` and `replay` compute what `steps` and `replays` allow ----

# THE CHECK, for a member: `guard` buries the note exactly when `same` said the member owns it
rule ownership-of-replay-own
  take at, like natural
  take whose, like natural
  take i, like natural
  take f, like flag
  take ev
    like same-view
      head
        read i
      head
        read whose
      head
        read f
  like settles
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, make member
    head
      read at
    head
      guard
        read f
        read at
        read whose
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, make member

task ownership-of-replay-own
  take at
  take whose
  take i
  take f
  take ev
  sift ev
    case is-same
      back
        make hit
          bind at, at
          bind whose, k
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, k
              bind rank, make member
          bind allowed-by
            make as-owner
              bind w, k
              bind r, make member
    case not-same
      back
        make keep
          bind at, at
          bind whose, b
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, a
              bind rank, make member
          bind aim, at

# THE POLICY, as `may` answers it: an admin buries any note, a member only their own
rule ownership-of-replay-may
  take at, like natural
  take whose, like natural
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  like settles
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      read at
    head
      guard
        may
          make person
            bind id, i
            bind rank, r
          read whose
        read at
        read whose
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r

task ownership-of-replay-may
  take at
  take whose
  take i
  take r
  sift r
    case admin
      back
        make hit
          bind at, at
          bind whose, whose
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, make admin
          bind allowed-by
            make as-admin
              bind i, i
              bind w, whose
    case member
      back ownership-of-replay-own(at, whose, i, same(i, whose), view-same(i, whose))

# THE AIM: the note is the one named exactly when `same` said so
rule ownership-of-replay-aim
  take at, like natural
  take whose, like natural
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  take id, like natural
  take f, like flag
  take ev
    like same-view
      head
        read at
      head
        read id
      head
        read f
  like settles
    head
      make live
        bind at, at
        bind whose, whose
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      read id
    head
      aim
        read f
        read at
        read whose
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r

task ownership-of-replay-aim
  take at
  take whose
  take i
  take r
  take id
  take f
  take ev
  sift ev
    case is-same
      back ownership-of-replay-may(k, whose, i, r)
    case not-same
      back
        make keep
          bind at, a
          bind whose, whose
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
          bind aim, b

# ONE NOTE: what `settle` computes is a settling `settles` allows
rule ownership-of-replay-settle
  take n, like note
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  take id, like natural
  like settles
    head
      read n
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      read id
    head
      settle
        read n
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
        read id

task ownership-of-replay-settle
  take n
  take i
  take r
  take id
  sift n
    case live
      back ownership-of-replay-aim(at, whose, i, r, id, same(at, id), view-same(at, id))
    case gone
      back
        make still
          bind at, at
          bind whose, whose
          bind by, by
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
          bind aim, id

# THE WHOLE SHELF: what `cross` computes is a crossing `crosses` allows
rule ownership-of-replay-cross
  take s, like shelf
  take i, like natural
  take r, like rank
  take id, like natural
  like crosses
    head
      read s
    head
      make person
        bind id, i
        bind rank, r
    head
      read id
    head
      cross
        read s
        make person
          bind id, i
          bind rank, r
        read id

task ownership-of-replay-cross
  take s
  take i
  take r
  take id
  sift s
    case bare
      back
        make cross-end
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
          bind aim, id
    case more
      back
        make cross-on
          bind top, top
          bind rest, rest
          bind doer
            make person
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
          bind aim, id
          bind top-after
            settle
              read top
              make person
                bind id, i
                bind rank, r
              read id
          bind rest-after
            cross
              read rest
              make person
                bind id, i
                bind rank, r
              read id
          bind one, ownership-of-replay-settle(top, i, r, id)
          bind others, ownership-of-replay-cross(rest, i, r, id)

# ONE STEP: what `step` computes is a step `steps` allows
rule ownership-of-replay-step
  take s, like shelf
  take e, like event
  like steps
    head
      read s
    head
      read e
    head
      step(s, e)

task ownership-of-replay-step
  take s
  take e
  sift e
    case write
      back
        make wrote
          bind before, s
          bind i, who
          bind r, rank
          bind aim, id
    case erase
      back
        make erased
          bind before, s
          bind i, who
          bind r, rank
          bind aim, id
          bind after-erase
            cross
              read s
              make person
                bind id, who
                bind rank, rank
              read id
          bind crossing, ownership-of-replay-cross(s, who, rank, id)

# THE RUN: what `replay` computes is a run `replays` allows
rule ownership-of-replay-run
  take es, like events
  like replays
    head
      read es
    head
      replay(es)

task ownership-of-replay-run
  take es
  sift es
    case begin
      back make from-start
    case after
      back
        make then
          bind last, event
          bind sooner, earlier
          bind was, replay(earlier)
          bind now, step(replay(earlier), event)
          bind reached, ownership-of-replay-run(earlier)
          bind stepped, ownership-of-replay-step(replay(earlier), event)

# LAW 1 OF THE TASK: after any events, every note `replay` computes as erased was erased by its owner or an admin
rule ownership-of-replay
  take es, like events
  like fair-shelf
    head
      replay(es)

task ownership-of-replay
  take es
  back ownership(es, replay(es), ownership-of-replay-run(es))
